{
  // Safari navigation -> Largest Contentful Paint probe.
  //
  // Safari/WebKit does NOT emit Chromium Perfetto traces, so the Chrome path's
  // perfetto + trace_processor LCP metric cannot work here. Instead we read LCP
  // straight from the page via a `largest-contentful-paint` PerformanceObserver
  // (the Web Vitals LCP API), using crossbench's browser-agnostic `js` probe.
  //
  // Timing note (important): the `js` probe's metric code runs in the probe's
  // stop() hook, i.e. AFTER the loading story's core workload has finished, with
  // the browser still on the loaded page. It therefore MUST run on the target
  // page, NOT on about:blank. That is why test-safari.sh does NOT pass
  // --about-blank-duration: doing so would navigate away before this code runs
  // and clear the page's performance timeline, yielding no LCP. (Chrome needs
  // about:blank to *finalize* LCP into its trace; the JS reading below does not
  // need finalization — the largest LCP candidate observed during the load is
  // the LCP.)
  //
  // Why a PerformanceObserver and not getEntriesByType: LCP is NOT exposed via
  // performance.getEntriesByType("largest-contentful-paint") on ANY browser —
  // that call returns []. LCP is only reachable through a PerformanceObserver.
  // We register one with { buffered: true }, which replays the entries that
  // fired during the load (before the observer existed) from the performance
  // entry buffer. Per the Performance Timeline spec, observe() with buffered
  // queues those past entries into the observer buffer synchronously, and
  // takeRecords() returns that buffer — so a single synchronous turn is enough.
  // This matters because crossbench drives Safari via WebDriver execute_script,
  // which does NOT await a returned Promise; an async read would never resolve.
  // (setup can't help: the `js` probe's setup runs pre-navigation on about:blank
  // and any observer it registers is destroyed by the navigation to the site.)
  //
  // Output: a flattened js.json per repetition containing:
  //   lcp_ms    - navigation -> LCP in milliseconds (or -1 if no LCP entry)
  //   lcp_count - number of LCP candidate entries observed (0 => -1 lcp_ms)
  "probes": {
    "js": {
      "js":
        '''
        const times = [];
        // Per spec startTime == renderTime (or loadTime when renderTime is
        // unavailable, e.g. a cross-origin image without Timing-Allow-Origin).
        // Fall back defensively so a 0/undefined field never masks a real LCP.
        const record = (e) => times.push(e.startTime || e.renderTime || e.loadTime || 0);
        const obs = new PerformanceObserver((list) => list.getEntries().forEach(record));
        obs.observe({ type: "largest-contentful-paint", buffered: true });
        // buffered:true fills the observer buffer synchronously; drain it here.
        // (The callback above is belt-and-suspenders in case a UA dispatches it
        // synchronously — execute_script won't run it on a later task.)
        obs.takeRecords().forEach(record);
        obs.disconnect();
        if (times.length === 0) {
          return { lcp_ms: -1, lcp_count: 0 };
        }
        // LCP is the largest/latest candidate.
        return { lcp_ms: Math.max(...times), lcp_count: times.length };
        '''
    }
  }
}
